+# Self-Referential Structures
+
+Validation follows pointers, slices, maps and interfaces, so a struct that is
+reachable from itself - a node with a parent pointer, a graph, a doubly linked
+list - forms a cycle. Each struct value is validated once per path: when a value
+already being validated on the current path is reached again, the traversal stops
+there rather than descending forever. The reported errors are unaffected, because
+the repeat visit would report what the first visit already did. Reaching the same
+value twice by two different paths is not a cycle and is validated both times.
+
 # Singleton
 
 Validator is designed to be thread-safe and used as a singleton instance.
